The provided class `CompletableEmpty` is a trivial, stateless singleton that immediately completes a `CompletableObserver` via `EmptyDisposable.complete`. It contains no computational logic, state changes, or I/O that could exhibit measurable performance characteristics. Benchmarking such a no-op operation would yield results dominated by JVM warm‑up and measurement overhead, offering little practical insight. Therefore, generating a JMH benchmark for this code is unnecessary.